    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Re-checked 2026-11-01 at 9ae4abe13f. The method-vs-function half is fixed: WI-barip (974edbe14d, 2026-10-19) keys methods by qualified name. In a fixture with def index plus Admin.index, path(\"\", index) resolves to the function. Nested classes are still keyed by bare name (py.py ~3566). A top-level LoginView followed by Outer.LoginView, with path(\"login/\", LoginView.as_view()), gives a UsageContext symbol_ref pointing at the nested class (urls.py:19-20). The dispatches_to edge pointed at the correct class (9-10). Volume is still unmeasured. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nSibling-of WI-jafat (reader-half call-ownership). The flat bare-/short-name-keyed, last-write-wins symbol_by_name dict has a SECOND consumer beyond call-graph resolution: framework route/view resolution (py.py Django ~848/861/866, DRF ~1223/1284/1298, Flask ~1443) resolves view_name/resource_name to a node.id (the DST of route edges) by bare name. A same-named view/handler across scopes (e.g. a method bare-key clobbering a same-named top-level function/class) can misattribute the route edge's target.\n\nCollision surface is strictly narrower than the call-graph method path: two same-name top-level defs in one module is illegal Python (runtime last-def-wins), so exploitable collisions are cross-kind/cross-scope only. VOLUME UNMEASURED — no out-of-span route-edge count exists in any analysis.\n\nGATE on a directed route-view collision probe (two same-named handlers — one top-level fn, one method — both route-registered) before implementing. Identity-neutral when fixed (re-attributes the dst edge endpoint only; no Symbol.id/stable_id/shape_id change). Source: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pypy_scope_rewrite_codesign_06142026.md (Phase 3)."  # 7aab
